      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Toxicity: RHS says all parts are poisonous, keep from children and pets; NC State rates severity low, says harm needs large amounts (nausea, vomiting, diarrhoea) and does not mention pets. Kept the higher grade (2) per rule 5; pet symptoms are mapped from the human ones. Skin 1: NC State says minor, short-lived irritation, repeated contact can give an allergic rash; RHS also says the sap irritates eyes (no eye symptom in our vocabulary, not graded). Light conflict: NC State wants some direct sun, RHS bright filtered light. Humidity conflict (NC State low to medium, RHS essential high): unknown. Size: NC State 2 to 8 ft (about 3 ft indoors) and RHS 30 to 90 cm, but no spread for houseplants: unknown. Watering mapped from RHS 'when the surface has dried'."
      },
